module System/Memory

### Every reader at once, no writer. The guarded entity is never changed, so there is no access to take: a
### `Guarded[T, ReadOnly]` is read directly (`g.name`, `g.label()`), and `ReadOnly` is a zero-sized record, so the
### manager's `access` member variable adds nothing. This is the default policy.
### :see: {AccessPolicy}, {Guarded}
record ReadOnly
obeys AccessPolicy
    nothing

### The AccessManager's kind for this policy: none, there is nothing to take.
### :returns: 0.
@readonly
routine ReadOnly.access_kind() -> U32
    return 0
